  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `get_thread_infeed` and `set_thread_infeed` for Threading operations.\nRead every plan field, including defaults.\nAccept partial updates through `EditOperationParams` as one undo step.\nSupport alternating flank infeed, spring passes and `repeat_each_depth`.\nRefuse unknown fields, malformed values and invalid plans by name.\nAdd the MCP skill row and the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\nMCP had no dedicated thread infeed tools.\nThe generic editor uses project JSON, which omits default plans and flags.\nIts field check rejects some resets to default values.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe three pins failed on unchanged production code before the fix.\nAll three pass with the fix:\n\n- `thread_infeed_tools_are_listed`\n- `thread_infeed_edits_read_back_and_undo_redo_restores_the_plan`\n- `thread_infeed_refuses_bad_fields_and_values_without_changing_the_plan`\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Restore `tools.rs` from `upstream/main`: all three pins fail. Restore the fix: all three pass.\n- Bypass the unknown-field check: the refusal pin fails. Restore the check: it passes.\n- Decode the previous plan instead of the candidate: the refusal pin fails. Restore the decoder: it passes.\n- Bypass command validation for minimum depth: the refusal pin fails. Restore validation: it passes.\n- Accept a missing or malformed plan as an empty patch: the refusal pin fails. Restore the check: it passes.\n- Treat another operation kind as Threading: the refusal pin fails. Restore the check: all three pins pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 116 steps passed, zero failed.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\nThe inherited sccache wrapper stalled during the first build.\nThe checks completed with that wrapper disabled.\n\nReview follow-up on head `5413cce6a9062c0980b87ddf9bce302ad6f5a59e`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: all 184 steps passed, zero failed. The full run completed in 31.4 minutes.\n- The heavy run used base `495ef74789b06f9aeaab09a18dd08c9b8ef06a20`.\n- The release build and all 183 selected app heavy targets completed, including lib, bins, integration targets and doc.\n- Twenty targets executed 42 heavy tests. All 42 passed, with zero failures.\n- Completed targets with heavy tests: `lib`, `adaptive_fig8_crossing`, `adaptive_pinch`, `carried_engine_agreement`, `feature_pick_wire`, `import_solidcraft`, `large_models`, `lathe_field_sim`, `lathe_workholding_kinds`, `operations`, `pick_agnostic`, `pocket3d_hsm`, `rotary_field_parity`, `shared_face_bodies_finish`, `shoulder_adaptive`, `stock_engine_agreement`, `stock_field_cost`, `stock_play_precalc`, `verify`, `whole_model_pocket`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: all 116 steps passed. Tests: 994 passed, zero failed, 10 ignored.\n- The quick run used base `76186e5c4fb5f75b374be0f66b56fca495aa4e4a`. Another session updated the local base ref during verification.\n- The PR head stayed unchanged. Both gates selected the same targets as the review.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed again on this head.\n- No source fix was required. The review had already confirmed the existing mutation checks.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` has no output.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe live GUI, physical machining and the release gate were not exercised.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #2773 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It changes `s_stock` and the stock skill row.\n- PR #2716 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It changes geometry tool descriptions and geometry skill rows.\n- PR #2678 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It adds protected-geometry tools and their module declaration.\n- PR #2554 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It changes `s_post` and a post-view module declaration.\n- PR #2149 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes. It adds protected-geometry tools and their module declaration.\n\nThese PRs do not change `all()` or the new handler module.\n\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: MCP reads and edits thread infeed plans, including alternating flank infeed, spring passes and repeat-each-depth settings.\n\nFixes #1847\n\n",
